  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:zombie-game:v0.1:action_rally">
    <zg:mayCause rdf:resource="urn:zombie-game:v0.1:CommunicationEffect"/>
    <zg:mayCause rdf:resource="urn:zombie-game:v0.1:RalliedEffect"/>
    <zg:cooldown rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">20.0</zg:cooldown>
    <zg:target_kind>SelfOrBroadcast</zg:target_kind>
    <rdfs:label>rally</rdfs:label>
    <zg:coverage>PARTIAL: typed baseline parameters and shared checks; full behavioral coverage is listed in coverage.json.</zg:coverage>
    <zg:capability rdf:resource="urn:zombie-game:v0.1:cap_rally"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:zombie-game:v0.1:ActionDefinition"/>
    <zg:sourceText>| `rally` | Broadcast from self. Duration 2 s; 15 stamina; cooldown 20 s. At completion, all other living zombies within `rally_radius` (30 m), including across barriers, gain `rally_hit_bonus` (0.10) for `rally_duration` (10 s). It is a signal-like effect; recipients choose their own actions. The Tyrant receives no hidden recipient identities in its result. A simultaneous radius-30, TTL-10 noise/signal cue follows Section 3.4. |</zg:sourceText>
    <zg:duration_min rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2.0</zg:duration_min>
    <zg:duration_max rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2.0</zg:duration_max>
    <zg:stamina_cost rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">15.0</zg:stamina_cost>
  </rdf:Description>
